  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Provision of lifesaving sexual and reproductive health services, gender-based violence response, and mental health and psychosocial support to vulnerable people affected by Cyclone Mocha</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The main objective of this project is to ensure that cyclone-affected women, girls, and young people have increased access to quality, integrated SRH, GBV and mental health and psychosocial support (MHPSS) services. This UNFPA provides life-saving SRHR services to affected populations, including persons with disabilities, procurement and distribution of clean delivery kits and other maternal health/family planning commodities, and recruitment and support of midwives to provide SRH services in the affected areas, among other activities. The project provides life-saving assistance to 74,727 people, including 46,447 women, 10,782 men, 9,993 children, and 3,429 persons with disabilities.</narrative>
  </description>
